      "properties": {
        "project_name": "500 Terry A. Francois Boulevard",
        "site": "Mission Bay South",
        "status": "complete",
        "use": "commercial",
        "geometry_type": "real",
        "digitized_from": "DataSF Assessor parcels (acdm-wktn), lot 8721010 (mapped 2001-03-20; active); the earlier outline came from: DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8721010, all 3 real footprint pieces within this Assessor lot unioned)",
        "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-19 for Mission Bay's third real-buildings pass (remaining uncovered footprints inside the official Mission Bay North/South redevelopment-area boundary): 500 Terry A. Francois Blvd (Mission Bay Block 26A), a 6-story, ~310,000 sq ft office building built by the Sobrato Organization, completed 2008; sat empty for four years before Cisco's Meraki division leased space in 2012, followed by Cisco's $1.2B acquisition of Meraki. Tenants have included Cisco and Wix. CORRECTED 2026-09-19: this file originally used only 1 of 3 real DataSF footprint pieces sharing mblr SF8721010 (the smallest, ~1172 sq m) -- a satellite-imagery cross-check prompted by the owner questioning apparent gaps elsewhere on the map led to a systematic real-city-block coverage audit, which caught this building's own incomplete geometry. Corrected to the union of all 3 pieces (~8636 sq m total), matching the ~310,000 sq ft / 6-story building described in sourcing. 2026-09-29 accuracy audit: 'Tenants have included Cisco and Wix' above -- Cisco (Meraki) is supported by the cited SF Chronicle coverage, but Wix appears in no cited source and is withdrawn. REPLACED 2026-10-12 (shape; status and use unchanged): the owner approved building records whose outline matches an Assessor lot at 85% or better, both ways, using the lot (CLAUDE.md, 'An official parcel beats our drawing'). DataSF's Assessor layer (data/raw/parcels.geojson) has Assessor lot 8721010 (7,485 m2, active, mapped 2001-03-20); the earlier outline of 5,383 m2 and the lot overlap with IoU 0.69 (98% of the earlier outline lies inside the lot and it covers 70% of the lot). The outline is now that lot using the lots' own vertices (no simplification). geometry_type stays 'real'. Previous digitized_from: 'DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8721010, all 3 real footprint pieces within this Assessor lot unioned)'. Previous accuracy_caveat: 'REAL -- surveyed DataSF Building Footprints outline (mblr SF8721010), cross-referenced by position against an OpenStreetMap building/address point (way 28844040) for the name and street address; not a hand trace or plan estimate. '. Previous notes: ' GEOMETRY CORRECTED 2026-09-19: previously only captured 1 of 3 real footprint pieces; now unioned.'.",
        "accuracy_caveat": "REAL lot geometry -- the outline is Assessor lot 8721010 (7,485 m2, active), so its edges are recorded lot lines, not a surveyed building footprint: it includes any yard, setback or plaza inside the lot and can sit a little off the walls. Until 2026-10-12 this record showed the surveyed building footprint (DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8721010, all 3 real footprint pieces within this Assessor lot unioned)); 98% of that outline lies inside the lot and it covered 70% of the lot.",
